---
source: crates/togi/tests/cli/mod.rs
expression: stdout(&ran)
---
Finds and tests per-core Curve Optimizer offsets on Zen 5 desktop CPUs

Usage: togi [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run             Start or resume the night's tuning session in the foreground
  day             Apply stock, observe daily use, pause or freeze, and report crashes
  completion      Print a shell completion script
  doctor          Check whether this machine is ready for a run
  events          Print the journal, one readable line per event
  night           Reboot into the tuning boot for the night
  night-end       Restore the day's boot selection
  reset           Archive the whole session
  restart-limit   Recover after the tuning service reaches its restart limit
  emergency-stop  Internal emergency recovery that stops leftover trials and sets every core to offset 0
  status          Show the session at a glance
  watch           Show the session dashboard with rootless stock-only day controls
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --state-dir <path>  State directory [default: /var/lib/togi]
  -h, --help              Print help
  -V, --version           Print version

Examples:
  sudo togi run         Tune this machine tonight until you stop it or a dead end does
  togi completion zsh   Print the completion script for zsh
